From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: make periodic wifi refresh timers asynchronous (onboarding blocker #2, Layer 2)

The map-agent uloop is single-threaded. The periodic per-BSS refresh timers
refresh_bssinfo() (bss_timer) and refresh_neighbor_list() (nbr_timer) called the
synchronous wifi HAL via blocking ubus_invoke(..., timeout):

  refresh_bssinfo      -> wifi_ap_status() / wifi_get_mld_stations() /
                          wifi_get_assoclist()
  refresh_neighbor_list-> sync_neighbor_lists() -> wifi_{get,add,del}_neighbor()

On mt76 affiliated-MLD / dynamic-4addr BSS the station-dump round-trip
(wifi_get_mld_stations -> nl80211 GET_STATION) can block for the full timeout.
Because the loop is single-threaded, that stalls uloop -> the map.agent ubus
object stops dispatching -> "map.agent status" times out at 3s -> no operational
BSS TLV is emitted -> the controller shows the node with radios:[] -> onboarding
never completes and nothing is persisted.

Convert both timers to asynchronous requests, mirroring the in-tree template
agent_init_wifi_radios() / ubus_call_object_async() / async_radio_status_success()
/ async_radio_timeout(): issue with ubus_invoke_async(), do the identical
post-processing in the data callback, and never wait on the loop.

Correctness:
  - per-BSS in-flight flags (bss_refresh_inflight / nbr_refresh_inflight) prevent
    the periodic timer from re-issuing while a previous async round is still
    outstanding (no double-issue, no state corruption);
  - completion and timeout are mutually exclusive (complete_cb does
    timer_del(&timeout); timeout aborts the request), so each request is freed
    exactly once, and out-of-order completion of the two chained bss stages is
    handled explicitly (stage-1 hands the terminal reschedule to stage-2);
  - every terminal path re-resolves the ap by ifname (agent_get_ap_by_ifname)
    instead of trusting a captured pointer, so a BSS torn down while a request is
    in flight is never dereferenced after free;
  - stage-2 selects object+method per BSS class exactly as the sync HAL does:
    "assoclist" on wifi.ap.<ifname> for a plain BSS, "stations" on
    wifi.apmld.<mld_ifname> only when is_affiliated_ap (the conditional used by
    wifi_ubus_get_assoclist/get_stas); this avoids the latent sync bug in
    wifi_ubus_get_mld_sta_links() that returns nothing for a non-MLD BSS on EM>=6;
  - the status data cb applies each field only when present (a missing optional
    field never aborts the station refresh) and only requires a usable BSSID;
  - on timeout/error we log and reschedule the timer -- the loop never wedges.

This is Layer 2 of the reliability fix. Layer 1 (libwifi warm cache)
makes the answers arrive fast; this layer makes map-agent not block its own loop
while waiting. Both are required for deterministic onboarding.

Supersedes the tactical skip in
patches/.../0004-mapagent-skip-wifi-probe-refresh-uloop-wedge.patch (drop 0004
when adopting this). Orthogonal to 0005 (bounded init loops) -- keep 0005.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
